  a_0 = 9.3624e-11 m/s^2

==========================================================================
PART 1 -- TWO STATES OF ONE CHARGE
==========================================================================

  PHANTOM   : g ~ a_0.  Generated by the baryons
              (div[f'(K) grad phi] = 4 pi G rho_bar), so BARYON-TIED.
              rho_ph = sqrt(G M_b a_0)/(4 pi G r^2);  M_ph/M_b = r/r_M.
  FREE DUST : g >> a_0.  Does not equilibrate, so it does not know a_0.
              COLLISIONLESS. Follows the galaxies, not the gas.

  [PASS] D1 [WHAT IT IS] the dark mass is the Noether charge of the scalar's
      shift symmetry, in two acceleration-selected states -- not a
      particle species
         measured: phantom (equilibrated, baryon-tied) + free dust (collisionless)
         Same charge, two states. This is why 40 years of direct detection have
         found nothing: there is no particle to find.

